\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Three regimes under optimization frictions ($\phi > 0$) across pre-kink income $z_0(n)$. Lower types ($n \le n_0$, gray) optimally remain at their pre-kink contract ($\Delta U = 0$). Within the potential bunching band $(z^*, z_0(n_B)]$, gross utility gains $\Delta U(z_0)$ (solid crimson curve) increase strictly with $z_0$ up to $\overline  {\phi } = \Delta U(n_B)$; agents below the indifference threshold $\underline  {z}_0(\phi )$ remain stuck at $z_0$ (yellow region, $\Delta U \le \phi $), whereas agents above $\underline  {z}_0(\phi )$ overcome the adjustment cost and bunch at $z^*$ (green region, $\Delta U > \phi $). Upper types ($n > n_B$, blue) adjust toward $z_1(n) > z^*$ rather than $z^*$.}}{18}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:p2_friction_regimes}{{10}{18}{Three regimes under optimization frictions ($\phi > 0$) across pre-kink income $z_0(n)$. Lower types ($n \le n_0$, gray) optimally remain at their pre-kink contract ($\Delta U = 0$). Within the potential bunching band $(z^*, z_0(n_B)]$, gross utility gains $\Delta U(z_0)$ (solid crimson curve) increase strictly with $z_0$ up to $\overline {\phi } = \Delta U(n_B)$; agents below the indifference threshold $\underline {z}_0(\phi )$ remain stuck at $z_0$ (yellow region, $\Delta U \le \phi $), whereas agents above $\underline {z}_0(\phi )$ overcome the adjustment cost and bunch at $z^*$ (green region, $\Delta U > \phi $). Upper types ($n > n_B$, blue) adjust toward $z_1(n) > z^*$ rather than $z^*$}{figure.10}{}}
